<title>USA: U.S. Aug leading indicators +0.2 pct - Conference Bd.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug leading indicators +0.2 pct - Conference Bd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1987=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    -			Index---Aug  July-Rev from  June</p>
<p> Leading Indicators    103.3   0.2    0.2   0.2     0.5</p>
<p> Coincident Indicators 121.8   0.4    0.2   0.1     0.4</p>
<p> Lagging Indicators    102.6   0.1    0.3   0.6    -0.2</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			    Aug   July-Rev from   June</p>
<p> Average Workweek	   0.04  -0.09  -0.13     0.04</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims   0.07   0.13   0.13    -0.01</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders   -0.03   0.08   0.08     0.01</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	  0.05  -0.08  -0.08     0.11</p>
<p> Plant, Equipment Orders -0.08   0.07   0.07    -0.02</p>
<p>    -			    Aug   July-Rev from   June</p>
<p> Building Permits	  -0.03   0.04   0.04    -0.04</p>
<p> Unfilled Orders	   -0.10  -0.04  -0.02    -0.01</p>
<p> Materials Prices	   0.18   0.15   0.16     0.20</p>
<p> Stock Prices		 0.08  -0.10  -0.10     0.03</p>
<p> Money Supply		 0.02  -0.02  -0.02     0.07</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations    0.01   0.04   0.04     0.09</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast a 0.2 percent increase in August leading indicators.</p>
<p>The August advance marks the seventh consecutively monthly rise.</p>
</text>
